@@ -120,6 +120,26 @@ $ rclone lsl --max-depth 1 :archive:s3:rclone/dir/100files.zip
 
 For `zip` and `squashfs` files this is 1s.
 
+## Symlinks
+
+Symbolic links stored in `zip` and `squashfs` archives are only
+exposed with the `-l`/`--links` flag, as with the other backends.
+They are then listed under their name plus a `.rclonelink` suffix and
+reading them returns the target path, so copying to a backend which
+supports symlinks (such as the local backend) recreates them.
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+Without `--links` the symlinks are skipped and a notice naming the
+flag is logged.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
